  "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Output one independent high-resolution RGBA transparent full-body game sprite, same 1254x1254 square canvas and camera as image 1, never a sheet or comparison. Image 1 is the sole edit target and character identity. Image 2 is user-approved same-direction running anatomy and relaxed arm mechanics only; do not copy the girl's face, clothes, bow, bare legs or palette. Image 3 is approved designs painting/material polish only; no UI.\nEdit only the two arms/sleeves/hands and the props they grip, to create a real intermediate arm-swing pose. Keep the exact face, closed small smile, head/topknot size and position, torso, belt, robe hem, hips, all pants/knees/ankles/boots and their pixel positions unchanged. Keep travel direction SE toward lower right. Do not translate or resize the whole figure. Anatomical RIGHT arm always owns the black-gold brush; anatomical LEFT arm always owns the ivory scroll. Trace each connected shoulder through elbow and wrist; a right arm may swing across chest but must never become the left arm. Exactly two arms, two hands, two legs, two cyan ink spirits, each spirit safely within canvas. Keep brush bristles attached axially to its shaft, exactly one teal tassel at brush HANDLE BUTT, not by ferrule. Preserve blank scroll with black/gold top-bottom rods and its lower yin-yang charm and teal tassel. Preserve the two ink spirits as the same pair near the moving scroll, gently follow its movement, never jump across the head or leave canvas. Charcoal trousers cover both legs. Keep all identity details and natural perspective. No extra fingers, duplicate props, frozen original hands, new footwear, ground plane, shadow, text or watermark.\nThis is run SE frame 03, preceding the forward right-brush arm swing in frame 04. In the 1254px source, move the anatomical RIGHT brush wrist from its current left-lower position near (410,770) forward/right to about (600,700), with elbow flexed naturally and connected to the near right shoulder. This visibly advances the brush hand toward the middle of the chest, neither leaving it at the original position nor swinging all the way to the far right. Simultaneously retract the anatomical LEFT scroll wrist from about (940,680) toward (760,680), close to the right-side chest, with far left shoulder and elbow connection clear. Let the scroll translate/rotate only enough to follow that grip and stay clear of the face. This is a moderate intermediate double-arm pose, not a full swap of props from right to left. Leg pose stays EXACTLY source03: one boot planted beneath body, opposite knee recovering upward. Keep the two spirits near the moved scroll without relocating them across the head.",
